RAM is monitored throughout every phase, not postponed until the end.

25. Definition of "Done"
V2 is not considered complete because the code is "faster."

A task is complete only when:

functionality is preserved
benchmark results improve
RAM does not regress materially
repeated operations remain stable
8-chart operation remains functional
no known regression is introduced
the implementation fits this architecture
26. Golden Rule
The following rule governs all future development:

Do not rewrite the architecture to solve an individual performance problem. Improve the component responsible for that problem while preserving the V2 architecture.

Any proposed architectural change must first demonstrate that the existing architecture cannot reasonably solve the problem.

